course: dictionary
lesson: 11012
title: Waterlogged: too full of water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Waterlogged means so full of water that it cannot soak up any more. Look at the words around it to check this.
explain: «Clay soil has tiny grains packed close, so it holds water and can become sticky and waterlogged.» The clues are holds water and sticky: the soil is already full, so it cannot take in more.
explain: Swap in your meaning to test it. "The soil is so full of water it cannot soak up any more" still makes sense, so you are right. Waterlogged can also describe a boat that is so full of water it is heavy or sinks.
fact: Waterlogged means so full of water that it cannot soak up any more.
fact: Waterlogged ground is why puddles stay on top after heavy rain.
fact: A waterlogged boat is so full of water that it is heavy or sinks.
fact: In science, waterlogged soil has no air, so many plants' roots can rot.
fact: After heavy rain, sports pitches can be waterlogged, and matches are called off.
exercise: «Clay soil has tiny grains packed close, so it holds water and can become sticky and waterlogged.» What does waterlogged mean here? | *So full of water it cannot soak up any more | Dry and dusty | Hot and cracked in the sun | Made of big grains with big gaps
exercise: After heavy rain, the football match was called off because the pitch was waterlogged. Why? | The pitch was made of sand that drains fast | The pitch was covered in snow and ice | *The pitch was so full of water it could not soak up any more | The pitch was too bright to play on
exercise: Which one is waterlogged? | A sunny field of dry grass | A dry sandy beach | *A boat so full of water that it is heavy and sinking | A glass of clean water on a table
test: Waterlogged soil has no air, so what can happen to many plants' roots? | They grow faster and stronger | They turn bright red | They dry out in the sun | *They can rot
test: Which phrase is an example of waterlogged ground? | A tall glass of clean water | A cracked, dry riverbed | A bright, sunny garden | *A waterlogged field after days of rain
exam: «Sandy soil has big grains with big gaps, so water drains through it fast.» Which word describes soil that cannot take in any more water? | *Waterlogged | Dusty | Sandy | Loam
